Data-source carve-outs (not covered by the blanket CC-BY-4.0 claim):

- Records derived from the Open Quantum Materials Database (OQMD) are subject
  to OQMD's terms of use, which restrict commercial use for a large share of
  entries. The OQMD connector is present in the pipeline but currently
  contributes zero records to the released dataset; if OQMD-derived rows are
  ever added, they must be flagged in `identity.source_db == "oqmd"` and
  excluded from the CC-BY-4.0 blanket grant. Do not assume OQMD rows are
  freely redistributable.
- All other source databases (Materials Project, JARVIS-DFT, NOMAD, AFLOW, COD,
  Materials Cloud) are covered under their respective terms; the Materials
  Project and JARVIS data are redistributable under their permissive licenses.
  Check `identity.source_db` per record before assuming redistribution rights.
